 "text": "Hi! How's life treating you? Everyone starts with no talent. The best way is to draw everything around you every day, for ten minutes, regularly. Start with simple shapes, like circles for heads, boxes for bodies, and sticks for limbs. Draw person standing in front of you, then next to it. The difference is you notice things when you draw every day. You start seeing the angles and the light. That's fine. Start with still life for a month, then people, then animals. Don't look at anyone else's drawing.",
